(3573158, 498208, 66597, '<td valign="top">This is underrated in my opinion. It has excellent composition and bokeh. I imagine you got hurt in voting due to large area of negative space. I commend your artistic choice here, however. Great entry.</td>', 'This is underrated in my opinion. It has excellent composition and bokeh. I imagine you got hurt in voting due to large area of negative space. I commend your artistic choice here, however. Great entry.', '2007-04-23 11:23:27.000000', NULL, 0),
(3573170, 497752, 43463, '<td valign="top"><table align="center" width="95%"><tr><td><div class="textsm"><b>Originally posted by KarenNfld:</b></div><hr/><i> Can you explain how you got the 1 pixel grey border almost all the way around? I can''t figure that out. </i></td></tr></table> <br/> <br/>Huh, I had not noticed that Karen. Now that you mention it, it is rather odd. I would attribute it to the large original file being resized down in one stop to 640X480.<br/> <br/>I went back to the two photos that I captured that are 7 seconds apart and virtually identical. The first one, I resized from the original file size of 3264 x 2448 down to 640x480 and did not get that 1 pixel border. The second shot that is virtually identical I resized and got that 1 pixel border. I did the test resize several times and got varying results that are driving me crazy. My photo was validated during the voting but I am now writing to the SC on this 1 pixel artifact border issue. <br/> <br/>Edit: Doh! When trying to replicate a problem one should:<br/> <br/>Don''t overthink.<br/> <br/>Make sure you get a good night''s sleep.<br/> <br/>Make sure you are following ALL the steps you did in EACH &amp; EVERY test :the missing factor that was not applied to all tests was the one time sharpening.<br/> <br/>RESULT: Resizing down from 3264 x 2448 to 640x480 then sharpen will result in that 1 pixel wide artifact border.<br/><br/><br/><i>Message edited by author 2007-04-23 12:07:46.</i></td>', 'Originally posted by KarenNfld: Can you explain how you got the 1 pixel grey border almost all the way around? I can''t figure that out.   Huh, I had not noticed that Karen. Now that you mention it, it is rather odd. I would attribute it to the large original file being resized down in one stop to 640X480. I went back to the two photos that I captured that are 7 seconds apart and virtually identical. The first one, I resized from the original file size of 3264 x 2448 down to 640x480 and did not get that 1 pixel border. The second shot that is virtually identical I resized and got that 1 pixel border. I did the test resize several times and got varying results that are driving me crazy. My photo was validated during the voting but I am now writing to the SC on this 1 pixel artifact border issue.  Edit: Doh! When trying to replicate a problem one should: Don''t overthink. Make sure you get a good night''s sleep. Make sure you are following ALL the steps you did in EACH & EVERY test :the missing factor that was not applied to all tests was the one time sharpening. RESULT: Resizing down from 3264 x 2448 to 640x480 then sharpen will result in that 1 pixel wide artifact border.', '2007-04-23 11:26:34.000000', '2007-04-23 13:07:46.000000', 0),
